    "q-96951": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96951",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A publisher has noticed that the minimum time needed to review a book is $115$ working days, and the maximum time is $235$ days. Assuming that the review time is uniformly distributed, what is the variance of the time needed to review a book?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the time needed to review a randomly chosen book. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[115,235],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[115,235],$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(235-115)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{14400}{12}=1200\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance of the reviewing time is $1200\\,{\\text{days}}^{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
